From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: neko-legends <neko-legends@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek_v41: faster prompt reading on four Sparks

- TF_DSV41_PREFILL_PIPE=<rows>: pipelined prompt reading (pipe.py). Each rank
  also holds a quarter of CED's encoder layers at full width (~27 GB a rank)
  and a long prompt's segments flow rank 0 -> 3 (in round t, rank s runs
  segment t - s). One exchange a round: the next stage's input (streams,
  the pending FFN post, the selection) point to point (NCCL p2p), the kv
  sources' new rows and the CED stash rows to every rank. finish_prompt and
  snapshots drain the line and spread the last-window SWA rows and carries.
  Decode is unchanged. 160k-token cold prompt 75 s -> 39 s on four Sparks.
  Own session tag (tag_grid + 2): a stage's layers run at world 1.
- TF_DSV41_INDEX_SPLIT=<rows>: an index layer's selection of a prefill
  segment computed for a quarter of the rows a rank and gathered (every rank
  computed every row's: the indexer's 32 heads are not tensor-parallel).
  Same selections, same bits; 160k 84.8 s -> 75.9 s without the pipeline.
- TF_DSV41_PREFILL_OVERLAP=<rows>: a prefill segment as two interleaved
  halves, each half's all-gathers on a high-priority stream behind the
  other's compute. Same bits; 20k 10.5 s -> 9.5 s.
- ppbench.py: the pipeline prototype and its layer-by-layer comparison with
  the tensor-parallel forward (--debug).
- tests: test_dsv41_overlap.py (overlap and split == one segment, TP4 and TP2
  replay), test_dsv41_pipe.py (a pipelined prompt == the tensor-parallel
  state in exact numerics: W = 2 and 4, a snapshot mid-prompt, p2p).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
